# Copy to scripts/remote.env and fill in your own SageMaker space (remote.env is git-ignored).
# The host name appears in ~/.ssh/config / the VS Code Remote-SSH window after you click
# "Open in VS Code" on the space page in SageMaker Studio. Format:
#   sagemaker-user@sm_dl_arn_._aws_._sagemaker_._<region>_._<account-id>_._space__<domain-id>__<space-name>
SM_HOST=""
